{
  "metadata": {
    "lastUpdated": "2026-07",
    "version": "1.0",
    "description": "Travel and vacation CPI indices for all 8 currencies. Covers airfares (COICOP CP073), package holidays (CP096), and accommodation services (CP115). USD includes BLS airline fares sub-series. Note: travel costs are among the most volatile CPI components due to fuel prices, demand cycles, and COVID-19 disruption (2020-2021).",
    "currencies": ["USD", "GBP", "EUR", "CAD", "AUD", "CHF", "JPY", "NZD"],
    "indexBase": "2015=100 for GBP, EUR, CAD, CHF, NZD, JPY. USD airline fares: 1982-84=100 native (BLS). AUD: 2011-Q3=100 native.",
    "sources": {
      "USD": {
        "airlineFares": "BLS CPI-U Airline Fares (CUUR0000SETG01), native base 1982-84=100.",
        "packageHolidays": "Not separately tracked in US CPI. Approximated from combination of airline fares and lodging away from home (CUUR0000SEHE).",
        "lodging": "BLS CPI-U Lodging Away from Home (CUUR0000SEHE), native base 1982-84=100."
      },
      "GBP": "ONS CPI Package Holidays (CP096) and Airfares (CP073), 2015=100. ONS CPI detailed reference tables.",
      "EUR": "Eurostat HICP Euro area (EA) CP096 Package Holidays and CP073 Passenger Transport by Air, annual average 2015=100. Dataset: prc_hicp_aind.",
      "CAD": "Statistics Canada CPI Travel Services and Air Transportation. Stats Canada Table 18-10-0004-01.",
      "AUD": "ABS CPI International Holiday Travel and Accommodation (COICOP CP096 equivalent). FRED AUSCP073000GYQ airline fares YoY and AUSCP096000IXNBQ package holidays index.",
      "CHF": "Swiss FSO CPI Package Holidays (CP096) and Airfares. FRED CP0960CHM086NEST and CP0730CHM086NEST.",
      "JPY": "Statistics Bureau of Japan CPI Package Tours. FRED JPNCP096000IXNBQ and JPNCP073000IXNBQ.",
      "NZD": "Stats NZ CPI International Air Transport and Accommodation. FRED NZLCP073000IXNBQ and NZLCP096000IXNBQ."
    },
    "notes": "COVID-19 caused extreme volatility in all travel CPI series in 2020-2021 (collapse then surge). Package holiday indices are particularly volatile. The 2022-2023 post-COVID recovery spike reflects pent-up demand plus fuel cost pass-through. GBP package holidays are heavily influenced by EUR exchange rates. USD lodging is separate from airfares and follows different dynamics."
  },

